  "rationale": "## Campaign Rationale – Actara 25 WG | Chickpea | September 2026\n\nThese nine segments — spanning Rajasthan, Bihar, Gujarat, Haryana, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Punjab, and Uttar Pradesh — were prioritised because the September 2026 reference date aligns with the **pod formation stage** in chickpea, a critical window for sucking pest intervention, and all 136 targeted growers carry propensity scores clustering between 0.315–0.347, indicating meaningful but actionable purchase intent across a combined base of 882 scored growers. **Actara 25 WG** was selected uniformly across all segments on a stage-aware basis, as its thiamethoxam formulation directly addresses aphid and whitefly pressure that peaks during pod fill, making timing the primary selection driver rather than scan-intent signals. The Rajasthan WhatsApp cohort (38 growers, highest score 0.347) was escalated to **offline reinforcement**, Maharashtra was flagged as **hot lead** given concentrated intent, and the remaining segments were assigned awareness-level messaging calibrated to their earlier funnel position — notably, **no OOS blocks were triggered**, meaning all planned segments can proceed without inventory substitution or campaign holds. Field teams should prioritise the Maharashtra hot-lead cohort and Rajasthan offline-reinforcement growers for direct rep follow-up within 7–10 days, while WhatsApp awareness pushes across the remaining six states are expected to advance mid-funnel growers toward consideration, collectively targeting a **15–20% conversion uplift** on the awareness cohorts and a **30%+ close rate** on the hot-lead and reinforcement segments given stage urgency.",
